      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. Problem: power outages, poisoned sessions &amp; black-box LLMs</h2>
          <p>
            Long-horizon desktop agent workflows without UPS hardware face three costly failure modes: (1) abrupt power loss corrupts monolithic state files or forces full-history replay that wastes thousands of tokens and repeats edits already on disk; (2) proprietary CLI backends leaving a <code>conversation_id</code> wedged in <code>interrupted</code> trigger <strong>10×–13× cascading retry failures</strong>; and (3) attempting to extract encrypted CoT traces violates provider ToS and fails across black-box APIs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="persistence">
          <h2>2. Split atomic persistence &amp; 15s durable flush (<code>workspace_state.rs</code>)</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Two-tier atomic storage:</strong> lightweight metadata in <code>workspace_index.json</code> (~20 KB) plus per-thread append-only logs in <code>sessions/&lt;id&gt;.jsonl</code>, written via temporary file + atomic rename (<code>atomic_write_bytes_inner</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Dedicated worker <code>cockpit-persist</code>:</strong> adaptively coalesces streaming writes (<code>220–1500 ms</code>) off the GPUI UI thread.</li>
            <li><strong>Power-loss durability:</strong> flushes to OS page cache every <code>2 s</code> during active streaming and forces explicit <code>File::sync_all()</code> on file + parent directory every <strong><code>15 s</code></strong> (<code>durable = true</code>), bounding crash loss to ≤ 15 s with zero JSON corruption.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="resumption">
          <h2>3. Git-Anchored Delta Resumption &amp; CLI self-healing (<code>app.rs</code>)</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Zero-token disk grounding:</strong> <code>continue_from_partial_turn</code> runs local <code>git status --short</code> (max 10 lines) and sends a micro-delta prompt containing only the trailing <code>300</code> chars (warm <code>cli_sessions</code> KV-cache) or <code>600</code> chars (fresh session) plus already-modified files.</li>
            <li><strong>Stale-session self-healing:</strong> on an exact Antigravity <code>interrupted</code> error, Cockpit clears <code>thread.cli_sessions[slot] = None</code> so the next resume starts a clean session seeded with the Git delta, eliminating repeated <code>interrupted</code> loops.</li>
            <li><strong>Credential classification:</strong> <code>UNAUTHENTICATED (code 401)</code> and <code>Eligibility check failed</code> pause the queue (<code>queue_paused = true</code>) instead of burning retries.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="fingerprinting">
          <h2>4. Black-Box Behavioral Fingerprinting (<code>telemetry.rs</code>)</h2>
          <p>
            Instead of inspecting hidden reasoning, every delegated turn logs only PII-free, code-free structure to <code>traces/trace_log.jsonl</code>: <code>Input (task_class, read_only) → tool_sequence (≤40, ! prefix on failure) → Outcome (pass@1, tokens, latency_ms, failure_signature)</code>.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Open-CoT vs. Black-Box split:</strong> automatically partitions <code>thinking_chars &gt;= 200</code> (open-weight reasoning models) from proprietary black-box backends under one schema.</li>
            <li><strong>Routing feedback (<code>analyze_behavioral_fingerprints</code>):</strong> exposed via <code>cockpit_benchmark_models(action:"traces")</code>, aggregating per <code>(model, task_class)</code> and emitting <code>behavioral_hints</code> whenever <code>runs &gt;= 3</code> and <code>pass@1 &lt; 60%</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="guards">
          <h2>5. Deterministic streaming guards &amp; 7-signature taxonomy</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><code>ThinkingLoopGuard</code> (<code>loop_guard.rs</code>):</strong> terminates circular self-doubt loops in <code>ThinkingDelta</code> upon <code>&gt;= 6</code> bilingual hedging cues or <code>&gt;= 18,000</code> continuous chars without tool calls; resets counters on any tool call (<code>record_tool_call</code>).</li>
            <li><strong><code>ConsecutiveFailGuard</code> (<code>loop_guard.rs</code>):</strong> hashes <code>normalize_error_signature</code> with 64-bit <code>FNV-1a</code> and triggers Fast-Escalate abort on <strong><code>2×</code> consecutive identical tool failures</strong> for <code>RLM-Cascade</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>7 mutually exclusive priority signatures (<code>classify_failure_signature</code>):</strong> <code>1. thinking_spin</code> → <code>2. consecutive_tool_fail_or_loop</code> → <code>3. timeout</code> → <code>4. blind_patch_no_read</code> → <code>5. repeated_tool_error</code> → <code>6. no_tool_action</code> → <code>7. unverified_or_exit_nonzero</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

